WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.023 --> 00:00:04.797
Roscoe had two mighty big problems to deal with.

2
00:00:04.798 --> 00:00:08.554
And he had just two days to get rid of them.

3
00:00:08.555 --> 00:00:13.719
"Are you going to fight the Tomato Brothers?" Mayor Wayne asked.

4
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.483
"Of course not!" Roscoe said.

5
00:00:16.484 --> 00:00:18.790
"We're going to arrest them."

6
00:00:18.791 --> 00:00:24.418
Cleo nodded. "If we fight them, we're playing by their rules."

7
00:00:24.419 --> 00:00:26.777
Mayor Wayne shook his head.

8
00:00:26.778 --> 00:00:28.936
"I hope you can lock them up.

9
00:00:28.937 --> 00:00:33.269
Rocky and Gus are pretty tricky."

10
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:35.997
"Don't worry, Mayor," Roscoe said.

11
00:00:35.998 --> 00:00:41.122
"We'll catch them."

12
00:00:41.123 --> 00:00:45.670
Roscoe and Cleo looked high and low for those raccoons.

13
00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:52.247
But for the rest of the day, things were quiet in town.

14
00:00:52.248 --> 00:00:55.667
They continued looking the next day.

15
00:00:55.668 --> 00:00:59.435
There was still no sign of the Tomato Brothers.

16
00:00:59.436 --> 00:01:03.428
"Maybe they left town," Roscoe said.

17
00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.458
Cleo shook her head.

18
00:01:05.459 --> 00:01:12.002
"They didn't leave. They're just hiding somewhere."

19
00:01:12.003 --> 00:01:15.899
A crowd gathered outside the sheriff's office.

20
00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:20.794
"Afternoon, folks. What's going on?" Roscoe asked.

21
00:01:20.795 --> 00:01:23.278
Buster held up the flyer.

22
00:01:23.279 --> 00:01:27.033
"We heard you're going to fight the Tomato Brothers tomorrow!"

23
00:01:27.034 --> 00:01:31.524
"I have rotten melons you can use, Sheriff," Sam said.

24
00:01:31.525 --> 00:01:35.034
Roscoe frowned. "Listen, folks.

25
00:01:35.035 --> 00:01:37.643
There isn't going to be a food fight."

26
00:01:37.644 --> 00:01:40.631
Everyone started talking at once.

27
00:01:40.632 --> 00:01:42.537
They were scared.

28
00:01:42.538 --> 00:01:45.007
Cleo held up her paw.

29
00:01:45.008 --> 00:01:50.676
"Don't worry. Roscoe and I will take care of those raccoons."

30
00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.450
Zeke spoke up.

31
00:01:52.451 --> 00:01:55.130
"The Tomato Brothers are awful!

32
00:01:55.131 --> 00:02:02.729
Nobody is safe until you catch them."

33
00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:09.137
It took a while, but Roscoe finally got everyone to calm down.

34
00:02:09.138 --> 00:02:12.049
The crowd broke apart.

35
00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:17.305
Roscoe and Cleo went into their office.

36
00:02:17.306 --> 00:02:21.771
Before they could sit down, Fritzy rushed through the door.

37
00:02:21.772 --> 00:02:25.626
"The Tomato Brothers attacked Mayor Wayne!"

38
00:02:25.627 --> 00:02:30.922
Cleo gasped. "Attacked him? Is he hurt?"

39
00:02:30.923 --> 00:02:33.916
"I'm not sure," Fritzy said.

40
00:02:33.917 --> 00:02:37.607
"He's in his house. You'd better come quick."

41
00:02:37.608 --> 00:02:42.316
They got there faster than a pebble flying from a slingshot.

42
00:02:42.317 --> 00:02:46.039
"What a mess!" Cleo cried.

43
00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:50.103
Mayor Wayne and his wife sat at the dining table.

44
00:02:50.104 --> 00:02:53.363
The mayor was covered in mashed potatoes.

45
00:02:53.364 --> 00:02:56.575
A bowl rested on top of his head.

46
00:02:56.576 --> 00:03:00.627
Dishes and food were scattered everywhere.

47
00:03:00.628 --> 00:03:03.995
"Mayor, what happened?" Roscoe asked.

48
00:03:03.996 --> 00:03:06.935
The mayor took the bowl off his head.

49
00:03:06.936 --> 00:03:10.469
"Those raccoons broke in and attacked us!"

50
00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:15.948
"They even stole my peach pie!" his wife said.

51
00:03:15.949 --> 00:03:18.638
The mayor pointed at the tablecloth.

52
00:03:18.639 --> 00:03:26.015
"They left a message for you and the deputy."

53
00:03:26.016 --> 00:03:29.131
The message was written in gravy:

54
00:03:29.132 --> 00:03:31.557
Tomorrow at noon.

55
00:03:31.558 --> 00:03:33.906
Okie Dokie Corral.

56
00:03:33.907 --> 00:03:39.922
No slingshots!

